    "commit_body": "Mirrors the v27 put WCF lift on the call side: when overall >= 75 AND weekly\nnon-confirming (wadj < 1), pull score down toward 55 by K=0.95 * weakness *\n(overall - 55). Closes the asymmetric-weekly-amp gap surfaced by miss-ledger.\n\nPer-trade evidence (experiments/miss_ledger/, 5y v31, 30dte_opt barriers w=15d):\n  85+ TP% +0.95pp / 80+ +1.09pp / 75+ +1.14pp ; puts unchanged ; N within H3.\n  Multi-window 75+: 1y +0.32 / 3y +1.49 / 5y +1.14 \u2014 sign-consistent.\n\nDiscriminator validation (experiments/miss_ledger/analyze_ledger.py):\n  wadj < 0 cohort on calls 70+: miss rate 52.5% vs 41.4% baseline (lift 1.27,\n  z=+10.1) \u2014 largest single-feature miss driver. Compounded with vsig=CONVICTION\n  to 56.1% / vmag=mid to 57.5%. Mirror surgically targets that cohort.\n\nCalibration (32 variants, fast_variant_runner):\n  K=0.95, wadj_cutoff=+1, score_gate=75, lift_target=55. Wider cutoffs (5-17)\n  delivered larger per-trade lift but collapsed N by 27-90% (failed H3) \u2014\n  that's a stricter gate, not alpha.\n\nAdds 'cwcf_dampen' to weight_info for explain-scores audits when active.\n\nCloses Priority #4 (Weekly Adj Smooth Scaling) in known-issues.md \u2014 though via\na discrete dampener in the wadj<0 cohort rather than a tanh-saturating amp.\nThe miss-ledger evidence concentrated entirely on wadj<0 (z=+10.1 for cut=0,\ndiluting at wider cuts), so the discrete formulation matches the signal shape.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
    "commit_short": "43eeceab",
